{"book":"pythagoras","bookTitle":"Theorem of Pythagoras","concept":3,"title":"Finding the hypotenuse","grades":"Grade 8","goal":"I can calculate the hypotenuse.","teach":"Square the two shorter sides, <b>add</b>, then take the square root: c = √(a² + b²). For 6 and 8: c = √(36 + 64) = √100 = 10. Round to 1 decimal place if the root is not a whole number.","tvis":"<div class=\"vis\"><span class=\"vi\"><svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" style=\"width:338px;height:auto\" viewBox=\"0 0 260 200\"><g transform=\"translate(20.0,20.0)\"><polygon points=\"20.0,20.0 20.0,140.0 200.0,140.0\" fill=\"#fff\" stroke=\"none\"/><line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"20.0\" x2=\"20.0\" y2=\"140.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"20.0\" y1=\"140.0\" x2=\"200.0\" y2=\"140.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><line x1=\"200.0\" y1=\"140.0\" x2=\"20.0\" y2=\"20.0\" stroke=\"#555555\" stroke-width=\"1.6\"/><path d=\"M20.0,129.0 L31.0,129.0 L31.0,140.0\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"#7A0000\" stroke-width=\"1.4\"/><text x=\"8.0\" y=\"84.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"end\" font-weight=\"bold\">6</text><text x=\"110.0\" y=\"160.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"middle\" font-weight=\"bold\">8</text><text x=\"122.0\" y=\"72.0\" font-family=\"Public Sans\" font-size=\"13\" fill=\"#7A0000\" text-anchor=\"start\" font-weight=\"bold\">c</text></g></svg></span></div>","ex":{"q":"Find the hypotenuse when the shorter sides are 2 cm and 3 cm.","steps":["c² = 2² + 3² = 4 + 9 = 13.","c = √13.","c ≈ 3,6 cm."]},"watch":"6² means 6 × 6 = 36, not 6 × 2.","qs":[{"text":"Shorter sides 5 and 12.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Hypotenuse","a":"13","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"√169","steps":"1. Formula: c² = a² + b², where c is the hypotenuse.<br>2. c² = 5² + 12²<br>3. c² = 25 + 144 = 169<br>4. c = √169 = 13"},{"text":"Shorter sides 9 and 12.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Hypotenuse","a":"15","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"√225","steps":"1. Formula: c² = a² + b², where c is the hypotenuse.<br>2. c² = 9² + 12²<br>3. c² = 81 + 144 = 225<br>4. c = √225 = 15"},{"text":"Shorter sides 8 and 15.","vis":"","parts":[{"t":"box","label":"Hypotenuse","a":"17","form":"val","o":null}],"hint":"√289","steps":"1. Formula: c² = a² + b², where c is the hypotenuse.<br>2. c² = 8² + 15²<br>3. c² = 64 + 225 = 289<br>4. c = √289 = 17"}]}